    {
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "intro",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Japanese signals give a **speed class** for the section ahead. On the TSW **Tadami Line** (single track, 65 km/h) the main signals have three aspects, **Clear**, **Caution** (45 km/h) and **Stop**, with a four-lamp **distant signal** before each station and **repeaters** where the view is short. The **JR East KiHa 40** runs under **ATS-SN** and the **EB** vigilance device. Busier JR lines add **Reduce speed** and **Restricted speed** on five-lamp heads (shown for reference). Quadrant controls are from TheJAG's KiHa 40 profile; \"gear lever\" means the Quadrant's gear lever (the KiHa's own gear is on the flap lever)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "systems",
          "title": "Safety systems",
          "cols": 3,
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ATS-SN",
              "full": "自動列車停止装置 S type, N variant",
              "summary": "A coil about 600 m before a signal at stop rings the **bell**: brake and press **ATS Acknowledge** (確認扱い) within **5 s**, or the emergency brake applies. The **alert sound** then continues. A coil **at** the signal brakes at once if it is passed at stop, and a departure coil does the same if you start against a starting signal at stop.",
              "where": "The whole Tadami Line in TSW",
              "quadrant": "**Gear lever** = ATS Acknowledge; **left aux** = ATS and EB power; **round aux** = Alert Release (警報持続解除)"
            },
            {
              "name": "ATS-P / Ps",
              "full": "Pattern-type ATS",
              "summary": "Checks a braking curve to signals and restrictions and brakes automatically; no acknowledge. On the real line Ps covers the Aizu-Wakamatsu and Koide station areas; **TSW simulates SN only**.",
              "where": "P: Tokyo area and main lines. Ps: JR East regional lines (Sendai, Niigata areas)",
              "quadrant": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "EB",
              "full": "EB装置 (Emergency Brake device)",
              "summary": "Above **15 km/h**, with no throttle, brake or horn movement for about **60 s**, a buzzer and lamp: reset within about **5 s** or the emergency brake applies.",
              "where": "Most JR trains, the KiHa 40 included",
              "quadrant": "**Left throttle button** = EB Reset"
            }
          ]
        },
