        {
          "kind": "howto",
          "title": "How to drive under ATS-SN and the EB",
          "cols": 3,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "title": "ATS-SN: approaching a stop signal",
              "steps": [
                "About 600 m before a signal at stop the **bell** rings.",
                "Brake handle to Lap or Apply, and within 5 s press **ATS Acknowledge** (gear lever).",
                "The **alert sound** continues: stop before the signal.",
                "Once stopped (or when the signal clears) press **Alert Release** (round aux), then drive on."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "ATS emergency brake",
              "steps": [
                "Passing a signal at stop, or no acknowledge in time: emergency brake.",
                "Brake handle to **Emergency**, wait for a complete stop.",
                "Press **ATS Acknowledge** (gear lever).",
                "Release the brake once the brake pipe has recovered; wait for the signal."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "EB (vigilance)",
              "steps": [
                "Above 15 km/h, moving the throttle, brake or horn resets the timer.",
                "After about 60 s without one the EB buzzer sounds: press **EB Reset** (left throttle button).",
                "Missed: emergency brake. Brake handle to Emergency, the warning stops; then release."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Before departure",
              "steps": [
                "**ATS and EB power** on (left aux): the self-test rings the bell for 2 s, then the alert sound.",
                "Press **Alert Release** (round aux) to silence it.",
                "Check the starting signal and the departure time, close the doors (RUD TRIM), release the brake, notch up."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Single track",
              "bullets": [
                "The Tadami Line is single track with crossing loops (Nishi-Wakamatsu, Aizu-Bange, Aizu-Miyashita, Aizu-Kawaguchi).",
                "At a loop the starting signal governs: wait for it to clear.",
                "The departure coil brakes the train if you start against it."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Speed",
              "bullets": [
                "Line speed 65 km/h; Caution 45 km/h.",
                "Speed signs set curve and points limits; higher speed only once the rear has passed the end sign.",
                "ATS-SN does not check your speed: brake to stop yourself."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "title": "Remember:",
          "text": "ATS-SN only checks that you acknowledged; it does not watch your speed afterwards. The coil at the signal is the last line of defence and stops the train at once."
        }
      ]
    }
